{
  "schema": 1,
  "app": [
    {
      "version": "1.7.5",
      "url": "https://github.com/SickIcarus-Labs/monitorbox-modules/releases/download/app-1.7.5/app-1.7.5.tar.gz",
      "sha256": "277bf41bc53ff56b45c8a550fce21b97739b2946f9dd53aa6bcece7e16c7c42b",
      "signature": null,
      "published": "2026-10-29T03:53:29Z",
      "channels": [
        "dev",
        "beta"
      ],
      "changes": [
        "A module is installed only when it is needed. A new box starts with Wake-on-LAN only (nothing can detect that you want it); a module such as UniFi, Portainer, Scrypted, SNMP or UPS (NUT) installs itself the first time you add or test a device of its kind, and a restored backup fetches the modules its connections use. The bell, the Update counts, Update all and automatic updating cover only modules you already have, so Hello on dev (or a module for equipment you do not own) no longer shows up as \"ready to install\". Boxes that already have modules keep them, and installing by hand from the Updates page still works."
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "1.7.4",
      "url": "https://github.com/SickIcarus-Labs/monitorbox-modules/releases/download/app-1.7.4/app-1.7.4.tar.gz",
      "sha256": "926f480058eb4ecd4593957b1fe12d67322aeeaabb2439ca9a80847d2e783ae2",
      "signature": null,
      "published": "2026-10-29T02:42:57Z",
      "channels": [
        "dev"
      ],
      "changes": [
        "Making a backup now shows up in the list as soon as it is done. Before, a slow backup (a full one) could leave the old list on screen until you refreshed the page."
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "1.7.3",
      "url": "https://github.com/SickIcarus-Labs/monitorbox-modules/releases/download/app-1.7.3/app-1.7.3.tar.gz",
      "sha256": "66fc72ea90f58d2a961324627d3c26c37710494f4ac738139872af63be9064a0",
      "signature": null,
      "published": "2026-10-29T02:26:38Z",
      "channels": [
        "dev"
      ],
      "changes": [
        "The Hello sample module is for the dev channel only. A box on beta or stable now removes it by itself (at start and when you change channel). It does not come back by itself; on dev you can install it by hand."
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "1.7.1",
      "url": "https://github.com/SickIcarus-Labs/monitorbox-modules/releases/download/app-1.7.1/app-1.7.1.tar.gz",
      "sha256": "6c0a9511d8b3182847df138b0458055ef96be8f8612e733c16539acc9a1779cb",
      "signature": null,
      "published": "2026-10-29T01:36:50Z",
      "channels": [
        "dev",
        "beta",
        "stable"
      ],
      "changes": [
        "Temperatures and drives are tidier and adjustable. On a card, three or more UniFi temperature checks fold into one line (\"UniFi temperatures \u00b7 3 temperatures \u00b7 all good\") that opens on tap, and by itself when one is hot, the same as the cameras and VPN tunnels. Protect drives fold the same way once there are three. Each device's or drive's warning limit can now be changed: open it, tap Edit monitoring, and set \"Warn when hotter than (\u00b0C)\". Empty uses the built-in limit (80 \u00b0C for a switch or gateway, 55 \u00b0C for a drive)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "1.7.0",
      "url": "https://github.com/SickIcarus-Labs/monitorbox-modules/releases/download/app-1.7.0/app-1.7.0.tar.gz",
      "sha256": "6f7f9d8ff40fc7b1f5a3c5dd954f4b749df30a4c506ad284d857f4a11dade6da",
      "signature": null,
      "published": "2026-10-29T01:25:55Z",
      "channels": [
        "dev"
      ],
      "changes": [
        "Three fixes to the main screen. The card history bars no longer go missing: the box built each card's 24 hour bar slowly (about two seconds on a Raspberry Pi when it was busy), so a request could fail and leave a card bare until the next minute or a refresh. It is now built many times faster, a bar that could not be fetched is asked for again within a few seconds, and a bar already on screen is never lost to a failed request. On the Updates page, \"Update all sites\" now appears as soon as \"Check all sites\" finds an update at a site, and goes away again when it is installed, without switching tabs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "1.6.44",
      "url": "https://github.com/SickIcarus-Labs/monitorbox-modules/releases/download/app-1.6.44/app-1.6.44.tar.gz",
      "sha256": "b217ebf78cd1c3ea65167a43f26830f4b04b376ed147e6e2fb0d925617b18754",
      "signature": null,
      "published": "2026-10-29T00:48:46Z",
      "channels": [
        "dev"
      ],
      "changes": [
        "The bell now looks for news every 15 seconds (it was every minute), and straight away when you come back to the page. It asks nothing while the page is not in front. A site that is slow to answer is never asked twice at once. An update on another site used to take up to a minute, after its restart, to reach the bell; now a few seconds."
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "1.6.43",
      "url": "https://github.com/SickIcarus-Labs/monitorbox-modules/releases/download/app-1.6.43/app-1.6.43.tar.gz",
      "sha256": "f16b7c60dbff8dfc75724ec502e2254d5a2931ad057df605c487c291c3c35625",
      "signature": null,
      "published": "2026-10-29T00:37:51Z",
      "channels": [
        "dev"
      ],
      "changes": [
        "A big update jump now shows a short version of \"What changed\" first. When a box is catching up on more than ten versions at once (a box on the stable channel, say), \"What changed\" opens with \"Highlights from N versions\": one short sentence for each of the changes we marked as the important ones, newest first, with \"Show everything\" underneath for the full list. A normal one-or-two-version update looks as before."
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "1.6.42",
      "url": "https://github.com/SickIcarus-Labs/monitorbox-modules/releases/download/app-1.6.42/app-1.6.42.tar.gz",
      "sha256": "dbe0423f2e2b3119df479c44c2a0c88f486063d368b3083ef001d7308654e43c",
      "signature": null,
      "published": "2026-10-29T00:25:00Z",
      "channels": [
        "dev"
      ],
      "changes": [
        "(#317, with UniFi Protect 0.1.3) New \"Drives\" checks for the recording drives in a UniFi Protect recorder. Re-detect offers one per drive; it shows the temperature (\"45 \u00b0C\") and reads Degraded at 55 \u00b0C or above (editable per drive), or when its bad-sector count grows, its health or state other than good/normal, or any fault reason. Bad sectors only warn when the count grows while the box is watching (a drive that has always had a few stays quiet). It uses the monitor's \"must last a while\" setting, so a brief spike stays quiet. A drive model Ubiquiti does not list (\"hddNotCompatible\") is ignored, as Protect's own screen does. A console that does not answer reads Unknown, never Failed. This reads one more page from the recorder (its own status, read-only)."
      ],
      "highlights": [
        "New drive temperature and health checks for UniFi Protect."
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "1.6.41",
      "url": "https://github.com/SickIcarus-Labs/monitorbox-modules/releases/download/app-1.6.41/app-1.6.41.tar.gz",
      "sha256": "9757a2e70d1e29c6ee3808d331750e8a876059901848d84c63a6e901ef6ebbeb",
      "signature": null,
      "published": "2026-10-28T23:56:25Z",
      "channels": [
        "dev"
      ],
      "changes": [
        "(#317, with UniFi Network 0.2.22) New \"Temperatures\" checks for UniFi devices. Re-detect offers one per device that reports a temperature; it shows the hottest reading and the fan speed (\"54 \u00b0C \u00b7 fan 31%\"), and reads Degraded when the device is at or above its limit (80 \u00b0C unless you change it) or says it is overheating. It uses the monitor's \"must last a while\" setting, so a brief spike stays quiet. A device with no sensor is not offered, and a controller that does not answer reads Unknown, never Failed."
      ],
      "highlights": [
        "New temperature checks for UniFi devices."
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "1.6.40",
      "url": "https://github.com/SickIcarus-Labs/monitorbox-modules/releases/download/app-1.6.40/app-1.6.40.tar.gz",
      "sha256": "b3fc38190294a761412622245c24937a25338723aea41c98bc7ce21d3b76c4ad",
      "signature": null,
      "published": "2026-10-28T23:45:26Z",
      "channels": [
        "dev"
      ],
      "changes": [
        "\"What changed\" now copes with a big jump, such as a box on the stable channel catching up many versions at once. It lists every version that has notes (up to 200), newest first, and leaves out versions released before notes travelled with releases."
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "1.6.39",
      "url": "https://github.com/SickIcarus-Labs/monitorbox-modules/releases/download/app-1.6.39/app-1.6.39.tar.gz",
      "sha256": "bf7fac1856fc6844271c7f742ab834ba8a860570156eae24d4d82b0a1fb1ae47",
      "signature": null,
      "published": "2026-10-28T23:18:20Z",
      "channels": [
        "dev"
      ],
      "changes": [
        "Tidier Updates page. The buttons now sit together in one row at the top: \"Check now\", \"Check all sites\" (only when a site is linked; it checks this box and every linked site and names any that did not answer), \"Update\" (only when this box has an update waiting; it used to be \"Update all (N)\", and the updates listed below can still be installed one at a time) and \"Update all sites\" (only when a linked site has an update waiting). The line of text beside the old Update button is gone."
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "1.6.38",
      "url": "https://github.com/SickIcarus-Labs/monitorbox-modules/releases/download/app-1.6.38/app-1.6.38.tar.gz",
      "sha256": "55d64648aed68ec0e9de26815366d81427af17c026d244a754e99460af575772",
      "signature": null,
      "published": "2026-10-28T23:09:17Z",
      "channels": [
        "dev"
      ],
      "changes": [
        "\"Update all sites\" now reloads the page when this box updates itself. Before, the page said \"This box is restarting\" and stayed there until you refreshed by hand; now it shows \"Restarting\u2026\" and comes back on its own, like any other app update."
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "1.6.37",
      "url": "https://github.com/SickIcarus-Labs/monitorbox-modules/releases/download/app-1.6.37/app-1.6.37.tar.gz",
      "sha256": "7bff628bd55ded9e9b4de322c4ec299e007d81af40aa21078b26a4a4bee78c07",
      "signature": null,
      "published": "2026-10-28T22:59:34Z",
      "channels": [
        "dev"
      ],
      "changes": [
        "The \"Update all sites\" button now shows only when an update is waiting at this box or at a linked site. It used to show whenever a site was linked."
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "1.6.36",
      "url": "https://github.com/SickIcarus-Labs/monitorbox-modules/releases/download/app-1.6.36/app-1.6.36.tar.gz",
      "sha256": "05e284c663cab2d096f7a1f00da76501db15465114face104ffb729a2d665108",
      "signature": null,
      "published": "2026-10-28T22:49:02Z",
      "channels": [
        "dev"
      ],
      "changes": [
        "History now names every port in a long Port errors stretch. A stretch used to keep only the ports named when it began, so a port that started rising later in the same stretch (like Guest Room, Port 8 at Broad Leaf) was never mentioned. Ports that join are now added to the reason, for example \"...; also Guest Room, Port 8\", up to the same length limit."
      ]
    },
    {
      "version": "1.6.35",
      "url": "https://github.com/SickIcarus-Labs/monitorbox-modules/releases/download/app-1.6.35/app-1.6.35.tar.gz",
      "sha256": "655f9aa3e4196fb1b5711b03d399df8eab634b482f98e9d9afd9b07235210295",
      "signature": null,
      "published": "2026-10-28T22:40:01Z",
      "channels": [
        "dev"
      ],
      "changes": [
        "The Updates page now has a \"What changed\" link on the MonitorBox app: when an update is waiting it lists what changed in every version between yours and the one on offer (newest first, in plain words); when you are up to date it shows what your version brought. The notes travel inside the release itself, so MonitorBox does not need to reach any other site. Versions released before this one carry no notes. Modules have no changelog yet, so only the app has the link."
      ],
      "highlights": [
        "The Updates page has a \"What changed\" link."
      ]
    },
